    "steps": [
      "Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion, salt and several grinds of pepper and sauté until soft, 5 to 8 minutes. Add the squash and cook, stirring occasionally, until it begins to soften, 8 to 10 minutes.",
      "Add the garlic, sage, rosemary and ginger. Stir and cook for 30 seconds to 1 minute, until fragrant. Add the stock, bring to a boil, cover, and reduce to a simmer. Cook until the squash is tender, 20 to 30 minutes.",
      "Let it cool slightly. Pour the soup into a blender, in batches if needed, and blend until smooth. If it is too thick, add up to 250 ml more stock and blend again.",
      "Season to taste. Serve with parsley, pepitas and crusty bread."
